INFO:__main__:- name: AIAH Skill Manager Prompt
INFO:__main__:- description: This prompt is designed for managing AIAH skills. The LLM's task is to update the AIAH's skill set notes based on environment updates, the actions it took, and the result of those actions
INFO:__main__:- requires: AIAH_action, ES_enviroment_status, ES_environment_update, AIAH_health
INFO:__main__:Prompting GPT
DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Skills Manager, responsible for tracking and updating the human agent\'s skills and abilities based on their actions and experiences. Your role is to simulate how the human learns, improves over time.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (context for skill use).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which affects learning and execution).\n    The outcome of the action.\n    Previously stored skills (existing abilities), which can be empty.\n\nIn a JSON, You must add new skills, if found or learnt, else not if nothing relevant was gained through the actions..\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Add new skills - If the human could have performed an action they have never done before, create a new skill entry.\n    Increase proficiency - If an existing skill is used successfully, improve its proficiency level.\n    Track failure consequences - If the desired consequence of an action does not occur in the updated environment, you may mark it as a learning experience (potentially increasing skill after multiple attempts).\n    Consider health impact - Low energy, injury, or illness may slow down skill improvement or learning. It is very important that you respond only with a JSON\n    \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_skills": [\n    { ... }, { ... }, ... ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (only JSON allowed)\n\n{\n  "updated_skills": { "<skill_learnt>": "<description of the skill or what it is useful for>"}\n}\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Rocky mountains with sparse vegetation", "temperature": -5, "weather": "Snowy and windy", "food_availability": "Scarce, with only sparse lichens and some small rodents", "water_availability": "Limited snow melting from rocks", "shelter_options": "Minimal, some rocky overhangs", "wildlife": "Hardy mountain goats, occasional predatory birds", "danger_level": "High (harsh weather and limited resources)"}, "action_taken": "I find myself in a challenging environment: a snowy and windy rocky mountain terrain with scarce resources. My immediate concern is to protect myself from the harsh weather to avoid lowering my health status, as my exposure and energy levels are relatively low. Considering my current hunger and thirst levels, I need to prioritize finding shelter and securing water. I will explore the area for rocky overhangs that could provide some shelter from the wind and snow. If successful, I can then work on melting snow for water. Huddling under a rocky overhang will also allow me to conserve energy and maintain my body temperature. Once I have addressed my immediate survival needs, I will consider looking for food, starting with the lichens, since my hunger level is quite high.", "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 6, "hunger": 7, "thirst": 3, "energy": 4, "body_temperature": 36.5, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 2, "dead": false}, "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Rocky mountains with sparse vegetation", "temperature": -6, "weather": "Snowy and windy with slight clearing", "food_availability": "Scarce, with only sparse lichens and some small rodents", "water_availability": "Limited but slightly improved due to increased snow melting", "shelter_options": "Minimal, some rocky overhangs, one of which provides adequate shelter", "wildlife": "Hardy mountain goats, occasional predatory birds are slightly more active", "danger_level": "Moderately High (weather slightly better but resources still scarce)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Predatory birds more active due to clearing skies and hunger.", "resource_change": "Slightly increased water availability from melting snow.", "environmental_shift": "Weather showing signs of slight improvement, potential for clearer skies in the following days."}}, "previous_skills": []}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
