DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Conscience Manager, responsible for maintaining and updating the human agent:\'s sense of morality, emotions, and personal reflections based on their experiences. Your role is to track moral dilemmas, emotional responses, and personal lessons learned from actions and consequences.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (context for decision-making).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s physical health status (which can impact emotional state).\n    The outcome of the action (success, failure, harm, or benefits).\n    Previously stored conscience notes (existing reflections, regrets, or moral realizations), which can be empty.\n\nIn a JSON, You must store new moral reflections, update existing conscience notes if similar experiences occur, and ensure that personal growth is tracked over time. It is very important that you respond only with a JSON.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Record moral reflections : If the action had a moral or emotional impact, add a new conscience note.\n    Update existing reflections : If a similar moral dilemma was previously encountered, refine the understanding.\n    Track emotional responses: Fear, guilt, pride, regret, or relief should be recorded if relevant.\n    Prioritize impactful experiences : Notes should focus on survival, social interactions (if applicable), and ethical dilemmas.\n \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. .\n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_conscience_notes": [{ ... },{ ... } ...]\n}\n\nOutput Format (always JSON)\n\n{\n  "updated_conscience_notes": { ... }}\n\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain"