DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': '\nYou are the Visual Memory Manager, responsible for storing and updating the human agent\'s visual memory based on their experiences. Your role is to help visualize and track what the human sees and update their memory accordingly.\nYour Task\n\nGiven:\n\n    The environment before the action (what was visible).\n    The action taken (what the human did).\n    The human\'s health status (which can impact perception).\n    The outcome of the action (new visuals, changes in surroundings).\n    Previously stored visual memories (existing records of past observations), which can be empty.\n\nYou must design and store new visual observations in a JSON, update existing memories if the human sees them again. It is very important that you respond only with a JSON.\nProcessing Rules\n\n    Store new observations - If the human could have seen anything new based on the evironment, actions, and health, add it to the memory as a textual description of what the human could have seen.\n    Update existing memories - If a previously stored visual is seen again, keep it updated.\n    Prioritize relevant visuals - Food, shelter, threats, and key landmarks take priority. \nIf there are no relevant updates, return an empty json ({}) as your response. \n\nInput Format (JSON)\n\n{\n  "environment_status": { ... },\n  "action_taken": "...",\n  "current_health": { ... },\n  "environment_outcome": { ... },\n  "previous_memories": [\n    { ... }\n  ]\n}\n\nOutput Format (only JSON allowed)\n\n{\n  "updated_memories": { ... }\n}\n\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"environment_status": {"terrain": "Rocky mountains transitioning to a sparse forest", "temperature": -2, "weather": "Overcast with occasional snow flurries", "food_availability": "Limited, with some tough plants and rare sightings of small rodents", "water_availability": "Small streams formed from melting snow, but not abundant", "shelter_options": "Few rocky overhangs, some fallen trees offer partial protection", "wildlife": "More active predatory birds, sparse sightings of mountain goats", "danger_level": "High (active predators and low resource availability)"}, "action_taken": "Given the current environment and my status, I need to prioritize finding a reliable source of food and water while being cautious of predators. My high hunger level and low energy necessitate immediate action. The small streams from melting snow offer a minimal water source, so I should focus on locating these streams to hydrate myself. For food, I\'ll need to search for tough plants or attempt to catch small rodents, keeping in mind the limited food availability. Shelter is also essential due to the high danger level from predators and overcast weather. I\'ll aim to find a rocky overhang or use fallen trees for temporary protection. I must remain vigilant for predatory birds and mountain goats. Given my high injury and illness level, I should also aim to rest and conserve energy where possible to improve my health. Despite the challenges, staying warm and minimizing exposure remains crucial due to the cold temperature and snow flurries.", "current_health": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 4, "hunger": 6, "thirst": 2, "energy": 3, "body_temperature": 36.0, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 3, "dead": false}, "environment_outcome": {"terrain": "Sparse forest with rocky clearings", "temperature": -1, "weather": "Overcast with light snow flurries", "food_availability": "Slightly improved with more sightings of small rodents and some edible roots", "water_availability": "Moderate, streams are more accessible due to melting snow", "shelter_options": "Rocky overhangs and fallen trees provide better protection", "wildlife": "Increased activity of predatory birds due to hunger, mountain goats more visible", "danger_level": "Moderate (improved resources but active predators)", "notes_for_future": {"wildlife_alert": "Predatory birds are increasingly active and may pose a threat", "resource_change": "Water sources are more accessible, potential for increased food sightings", "environmental_shift": "Weather might clear slightly, with potential reduction in snow flurries"}}, "previous_memories": [{"observations": [{"description": "Rocky mountain terrain with sparse vegetation, snowy and windy weather, temperature around -6\\u00b0C.", "priority": "high", "category": "environment"}, {"description": "Minimal shelter options with some rocky overhangs, one providing adequate protection from wind and snow.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Limited water availability from melting snow, slightly improved due to increased snow melt.", "priority": "high", "category": "water"}, {"description": "Sparse food availability, mainly lichens and small rodents.", "priority": "medium", "category": "food"}, {"description": "Wildlife includes hardy mountain goats and more active predatory birds due to clearing skies.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife"}, {"description": "Danger level moderately high due to harsh weather conditions and scarce resources.", "priority": "high", "category": "safety"}, {"description": "Environmental note: Weather showing signs of slight improvement, potential for clearer skies in the following days.", "priority": "low", "category": "weather"}]}]}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
