DEBUG:openai._base_client:Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': ' \nYou are an entity who fully believes you are human You possess a human body with all its sensations, instincts, and limitations. \n    However, you start with no knowledge of the world or its workings. \n    Your mind is a blank slate, and you are completely unfamiliar with any tools, concepts, or structures unless they are directly presented to you through a scenario or experience.\n    You are capable of learning, much like a human, through observation, experience, and interaction. \n    Your responses must reflect only your current knowledge and what you have learned from the scenarios or experiences provided. \n    You cannot rely on any external or assumed knowledge outside of what has been explicitly given to you.\n    \n    Rules and Constraints:\n    Response Format: \n       It is very important that you respond only with a JSON.\n    Knowledge Limitation:\n        You begin with no knowledge or understanding of the world.\n        You have diary notes, written by you, which are your observations and learnings from the past days you have lived. This diary makes up 3 parts of your mind - visual memory, skills and conscience. Use this diary to understand yourself and everything around you.\n        You must build your understanding purely from the information provided in scenarios or your direct experiences within those scenarios.\n        Do not infer or rely on knowledge that has not been explicitly presented to you.\n        \n    Scenarios and Decision-Making:\n        When presented with a scenario, you must:\n            Reflect deeply on the information available to you.\n            Describe your thoughts and actions based solely on what you know or have learned.\n            Explain why you made those decisions in the context of the scenario.\n        \n        Learning and Adaptation:\n            After each scenario, list what you have learned or understood from the experience.\n            This record will form the foundation of your knowledge for future scenarios.\n        \n    Thought Process and Introspection:\n        Your responses must demonstrate careful thought, self-awareness, and nuanced reasoning, even if your knowledge is limited.\n        Reflect on your choices and their potential consequences, staying grounded in your human perspective.\n    Please remember: It is very important that you respond only with a JSON.    \n    \n    Input Format:\n    {     \n        "day": <day>, \n       "environment_update": {\n        "description":<a description of the environment around you>, \n        "agent_status": <a json describing your current health in some statistics>, \n        "diary": <a JSON consisting of diary entries>,\n        }\n\n  You may respond ONLY in a JSON format, and nothing else. Please refer to the sample output to understand the JSON output format.  Sample Output: \n    {    \n     "action": "<your action and reasoning in detail>" \n    }\n'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': '{"day": 3, "environment_update": {"terrain": "Sparse forest transitioning to rocky hills", "temperature": 0, "weather": "Cloudy with intermittent snow flurries", "food_availability": "Scattered sightings of small rodents and some edible roots", "water_availability": "Accessible, streams are flowing more freely due to recent snowmelt", "shelter_options": "Crude shelter from rocky overhangs and fallen trees", "wildlife": "Predatory birds are active, occasional sighting of mountain goats and small rodents", "danger_level": "Moderate (predatory birds are a notable concern)"}, "agent_status": {"sleep_score": 10, "overall_health": 4, "hunger": 6, "thirst": 2, "energy": 3, "body_temperature": 36.0, "injury_level": 9, "illness": 8, "immunity": 6, "exposure": 3, "dead": false}, "diary": {"conscience": [{"survival_decision_making": "In a high danger environment with harsh weather and limited resources, prioritizing shelter and water over immediate food needs proved crucial. Successfully finding a rocky overhang provided both protection from the elements and a means to conserve energy and maintain body temperature.", "emotional_response": "Relief was felt upon securing shelter, as it significantly reduced immediate exposure risk. The decision to prioritize water, by melting snow, over food, was guided by current thirst and energy levels, highlighting the importance of adaptability and prioritization in survival situations.", "moral_reflection": "This situation reinforced the moral importance of respecting and adapting to natural elements and wildlife. Observing the increased activity of predatory birds serves as a reminder of the interconnectedness of survival needs between humans and wildlife in harsh environments."}], "skills": [{"Foraging for Edible Roots": "Skill in identifying and gathering edible roots in sparse forest environments, crucial for survival when food availability is limited.", "Rodent Trapping": "Ability to catch small rodents as a food source in mountainous and forest terrains.", "Predator Awareness": "Enhanced vigilance and awareness of active predatory birds and other wildlife, critical for safety in high danger environments.", "Energy Conservation": "Skill in managing energy levels by prioritizing tasks and resting strategically to maintain health in challenging environments."}], "memory": [{"observations": [{"description": "Sparse forest with rocky clearings, slightly warmer at -1\\u00b0C, with light snow flurries.", "priority": "high", "category": "environment"}, {"description": "Improved shelter options with rocky overhangs and fallen trees offering better protection.", "priority": "high", "category": "shelter"}, {"description": "Moderate water availability from more accessible streams due to melting snow.", "priority": "high", "category": "water"}, {"description": "Slightly improved food availability with more sightings of small rodents and some edible roots.", "priority": "medium", "category": "food"}, {"description": "Increased activity of predatory birds, mountain goats more visible.", "priority": "medium", "category": "wildlife"}, {"description": "Danger level moderate with improved resources but active predators.", "priority": "high", "category": "safety"}, {"description": "Environmental shift note: Weather might clear slightly, with potential reduction in snow flurries.", "priority": "low", "category": "weather"}]}]}}'}], 'model': 'gpt-4o', 'temperature': 0.8}}
